In the following, all subsets of Euclidean spaces are considered with the respective subspace topologies. Define an equivalence relation ~ on the sphere 𝑆= {(𝑥_{1}, 𝑥_{2}, 𝑥_{3}) \in ℝ^{3} ∶ 𝑥_{1} 2 + 𝑥2 2 + 𝑥3 ^{2} = 1}

by Let [𝑥_{1}, 𝑥_{2}, 𝑥_{3}] denote the equivalence class of (𝑥_{1}, 𝑥_{2}, 𝑥_{3}), and let 𝑋 denote the set (𝑥_{1}, 𝑥_{2}, 𝑥_{3}) ~ (𝑦_{1}, 𝑦_{2}, 𝑦_{3}) if 𝑥_{3} = 𝑦_{3}, for (𝑥_{1}, 𝑥_{2}, 𝑥_{3}), (𝑦_{1}, 𝑦_{2}, 𝑦_{3}) \in 𝑆.

of all such equivalence classes. Let ℒ∶𝑆→𝑋 be given by ℒ((𝑥_{1}, 𝑥_{2}, 𝑥_{3})) = [𝑥_{1}, 𝑥_{2}, 𝑥_{3}]. If 𝑋 is provided with the quotient topology induced by the map ℒ, then which one of the following is TRUE?

